iew-verdict-rev1.md; TASK-260916-n9r71p_results.md, _results-rev2.md, _results-rev3.md, the accepted verdict TASK-260916-n9r71p_review-verdict-rev2.md and the overlay re-validation TASK-260916-n9r71p_results-rev3-verify-RUN-260917-7d0bd5.md (37/37 packages green on a trunk-7efe385 overlay, tracecheck acceptance_cases=135 bindings=68 clauses_discharged=49/569, cataloggen -adopted -check exit 0).\n4|\n5|EXPORTED INPUTS (read-only, in the control root): .temp/v070-carry/checkpoint-2yzf5d.patch (the pin leaf's committed delta, trunk 7efe385 -> checkpoint 9cb5dd4, binary-safe), .temp/v070-carry/uncommitted-n9r71p.patch (the registry leaf's tracked delta against that checkpoint) and .temp/v070-carry/files/ (its three untracked files: internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json, internal/traceability/adoption-v0.7.0.md, internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json). Expected digests after reconstruction: sha256(internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json) = 2548870d896b0e119c307cdcba02ab23b36af7f473328a15f6a092090d8a5070 and reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = c4cd46bf71f164ad53dfe00ddd2e64e0b439e1c2684138fbcfe208f7e53473f6 — if your reconstruction differs, the difference must be explained and justified in the results, never silently accepted.\n6|\n7|DO EXACTLY THIS in your managed Story worktree (task-board provisions .temp/STORY-260917-110onn/worktree from current trunk; never touch .temp/STORY-260916-3uqbwq/worktree, it is a read-only historical artifact): (1) apply the pin patch, then the registry patch, then copy the three untracked files; resolve any context rejects by hand against the current trunk content and record every hunk you had to adapt; (2) re-verify, do not trust: `git tag -v v0.7.0` in a fresh read-only clone of relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec (tag object d4abe46fb12d9ba347c09f43efb01089530795b3, peeled commit 32b3f2ba7c377248a53cd42389abbd2f1c321834), SPEC.md LF sha256 c6b2fe64ee79ed697a96ed27a1679c80b8ee1eba137feb99e7738b4da289ddcf byte-identical to internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md; the v0.7.0 lock's 64 rows against the pinned document's contract table; ownership.v0.7.0.json against `git show 7efe385:internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` binding by binding with clause lines re-measured against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (every binding the five landed Stories added must be present: provhost identity/profiles/resumesmoke, sessckpt/matjournal/crashgate, lease store/fencing/ownership properties, hostchannel/rpcwire/AC-HOST-001, sections 2.4/5.3/5.4/5.5/8/10.6/11.10.x/13.12/13.13/16.1) plus the seven launch-plan Story-owner bindings and the Launch Plan request row; ownership.v0.5.0.json and ownership.v0.6.0.json byte-identical to trunk; (3) regenerate catalog_gen.go with `-adopted` and prove `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0; re-pin reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 over the registry you actually ship and refresh the tracecheck/report pins; (4) ADD the two verification tests this Story owes: a committed test that re-derives the v0.7.0 registry projection from the trunk v0.6.0 registry and fails on any missing binding, unshifted clause line or self-minted claim; and a committed test that pins the README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection (its fenced `section coverage:` line and prose figures) to the tracecheck report on the current tree — make the subsection equal the tool output byte-for-byte; (5) README/LOGBOOK entries truthful with no launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim (the section:11.10.5 gap says \"Disclosure owner\", not \"Pending implementation owner\"); task-board.config.json must equal HEAD; (6) run the full configured 27-command suite on the exact tree (command 5 `go test ./... -race` can take ~10 minutes under load; if it times out, rerun it alone and record both runs).\n8|COMMON CONTRACT (first leaf of a Story on trunk 7efe385 or later). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named below; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260916-3uqbwq) is landing during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) — never fork a second model; extend or adopt. Traceability: this Story IS the registry work — you own internal/traceability, the digest pin and the README measured-coverage subsection. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260917-110onn/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260917-110onn forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED; never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260917-10k118` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <REBASE_HEAD original checkpoint>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that appears in your git status and restore trunk content by hand (README/LOGBOOK purely additive; task-board.config.json == HEAD); before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured 26-command validation suite once before handoff (command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`); hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260917-10k118_results.md, TASK-260917-10k118_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260917-10k118_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260917-10k118 --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.","final_result":true}}}
