{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c62f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b074-2d9a-7d23-a683-c8d705b137ba"},"sequence":370,"recorded_at":1780531400000735,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b075-f2fe-77b1-81ec-bcc0156040bf"},"task_id":"01a0b075-f2fe-77b1-81ec-bcc0156040bf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b075-f2fe-77b1-81ec-bcc0156040bf","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager && git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4 -- LOGBOOK.md | head -n 60; echo \\\"===README-HUNK===\\\"; git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4 -- README.md | head -n 80\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect pin delta LOGBOOK and README hunks\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 0ee16ab..425f86a 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@\\n - TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n - DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n \\n+### TASK-260916-2yzf5d: adopted signed v0.7.0 normative source alongside v0.5.0/v0.6.0, no consumer re-pointed\\n+- PROVENANCE (verified this session, upstream read-only): `git tag -v v0.7.0` Good (tag object `d4abe46f…795b3`, ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM`, tagger Ivan Oparin), peeled commit `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC.md blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes SHA256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` measured from the tagged blob (zero CR bytes, raw == LF-normalized).\\n+- SCOPE: `internal/specpin/{pin,sections}.go` + `v0.7.0.lock.json` (64 contracts, 6 fixtures), `internal/specdoc/{specdoc.go,SPEC.v0.7.0.md}` + `pin070_test.go`, `sections070_test.go`, `specdoc070_test.go`, README provenance paragraphs, this entry. `v0.5.0`/`v0.6.0` locks, documents, readers and all existing tests byte-untouched in behavior.\\n+- DELTA (measured, SPEC §1.5 cross-checked row-for-row in order, lock registry verified against the spec table by script): +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (between Session record and Session event); Session record +3.1.0, Provider protocol +2.1.0/+3.1.0, Provider manifest/probe +1.1.0, Structured error +1.5.0, CLI result unchanged at 5.0.0; +0 numbered sections (only an unnumbered `#### Caller launch-plan code` and appendix subsection A.12, both excluded by the inventory rule — the 170-identifier inventory digest is measured equal to v0.6.0's and pinned independently); +1 fixture (`ax-launch-plan-request-v1` `ec4310b8…`), host-channel/selector fixture digests move for a `specification_version` 0.7.0 bump only, 3 old fixture files byte-identical upstream. v0.4.3 compatibility grows to 9 absent + 9 overrides exactly as the v0.7.0 historical account states.\\n+- HISTORY: v0.7.0 projections of v0.6.0 (63 rows), v0.5.0 (60 rows) and v0.4.3 (55 rows) are `reflect.DeepEqual` to the real locks/projections — adoption cannot rewrite history. `ContractsForRelease(v0.7.0)` on a v0.5.0 or v0.6.0 manifest is refused: a stale pin cannot authorize the new release. Launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift runtime support is not claimed; `catalog/`, `traceability/`, `cigate/`, `localstore/` untouched, `tracecheck` still 17/463, `cataloggen -check` green without regeneration.\\n+- MUTANTS (5 narrowing, each admits exactly one member end-to-end, each kills exactly its named subtest, full suites otherwise green, all restored snapshot-clean): M1 identity+stale-commit, M2 token-preserving delta-row Versions drop (full behavioral suite under plant), M3 ParseV070+stale-v0.6.0-doc, M4 projection serves v0.7.0 from stale manifest, M5 digest+trailing-newline; M0 harmless operand-swap SURVIVED. VerifyV070 is layered (validate then digest), so M1/M2/M5 span both layers with precomputed digests. Harness + raw logs in the task evidence tarball.\\n+- DEPENDENCY: catalogue/traceability regeneration is sibling TASK-260916-n9r71p, after this leaf checkpoints. `Current`/`Verify`/`Load` intentionally still serve v0.5.0; v0.6.0 consumers move with the sibling, not here.\\n+- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\\n - REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\\n   compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\\n===README-HUNK===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex da17ad5..631db34 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -79,16 +79,25 @@ planning authority.\\n [`internal/specpin`](internal/specpin) embeds one implementation lock for\\n `agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0`, plus the adopted\\n `agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0` lock (signed tag `v0.6.0`, verified\\n-before adoption). Its production `Current` and `Verify`\\n+before adoption) and the adopted `agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0` lock\\n+(signed tag `v0.7.0`, verified before adoption). Its production `Current` and `Verify`\\n entry points fail closed on a partial read, unknown member, source substitution,\\n contract or fixture drift, and any byte-level lock change. It also projects the\\n exact historical v0.4.3 registry without widening that immutable baseline.\\n The v0.6.0 entry points (`CurrentV060`, `VerifyV060`) enforce the same\\n closed policy over the 63-row prepared registry, and the v0.6.0 projections\\n of the v0.5.0 and v0.4.3 registries are proved row-equal to the real\\n-historical locks, so adoption rewrites no history. `Current` and `CurrentV050` retain the historical v0.5.0 baseline.\\n+historical locks, so adoption rewrites no history. The v0.7.0 entry points\\n+(`CurrentV070`, `VerifyV070`) enforce the same closed policy over the 64-row\\n+launch-plan registry, and the v0.7.0 projections of the v0.6.0, v0.5.0 and\\n+v0.4.3 registries are proved row-equal to the real historical locks.\\n+`Current` and `CurrentV050` retain the historical v0.5.0 baseline.\\n The catalogue generator, CI contract roots and traceability gate explicitly\\n-consume v0.6.0; localstore explicitly uses `CurrentV050`.\\n+consume v0.6.0 until their owning regeneration task moves them to v0.7.0;\\n+localstore explicitly uses `CurrentV050`. Adopting the v0.7.0 source claims\\n+no launch-plan, `SpawnPlan` stdin, `caller_launch_plan` /\\n+`stdin_resume_replay`, `environment_drift`, or curator-run naming runtime\\n+support; those remain pending owners outside this adoption.\\n \\n This package is read-only and does not mutate durable state. Repeated reads are\\n idempotent and isolated from caller mutation. It deliberately adds no `ax`\\n@@ -105,8 +114,11 @@ artifacts are supposed to constrain. The upstream specification remains\\n normative; this copy is a verification input and amends nothing. It\\n additionally embeds the byte-exact adopted v0.6.0 `SPEC.md` behind the\\n `LoadV060`/`ParseV060` entry points, which accept only\\n-`specpin.DocumentSHA256V060` and refuse the historical document; `Load`\\n-retains v0.5.0 for historical consumers; traceability uses `LoadV060`.\\n+`specpin.DocumentSHA256V060` and refuse the historical document, and the\\n+byte-exact adopted v0.7.0 `SPEC.md` behind `LoadV070`/`ParseV070`, which\\n+accept only `specpin.DocumentSHA256V070` and refuse both historical\\n+documents; `Load` retains v0.5.0 for historical consumers; traceability uses\\n+`LoadV060` until its owning regeneration task moves it to `LoadV070`.\\n \\n `Load` accepts the document only when its SHA-256 equals\\n `specpin.DocumentSHA256`, so a substituted, edited, truncated, or unreadable\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7228,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1807,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
