{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c693","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b074-2d9a-7d23-a683-c8d705b137ba"},"sequence":420,"recorded_at":1780531400000835,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b076-5031-7030-888e-02ee12853113"},"task_id":"01a0b076-5031-7030-888e-02ee12853113","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b076-5031-7030-888e-02ee12853113","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-14-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sha256sum /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/v070-carry/files/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json; echo \\\"EXPECTED: 2548870d896b0e119c307cdcba02ab23b36af7f473328a15f6a092090d8a5070\\\"; echo \\\"===\\\"; cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260917-110onn/worktree && head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Verify carried registry digest and LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2548870d896b0e119c307cdcba02ab23b36af7f473328a15f6a092090d8a5070  /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/v070-carry/files/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json\\nEXPECTED: 2548870d896b0e119c307cdcba02ab23b36af7f473328a15f6a092090d8a5070\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n  resolution — select the greatest tuple first, then report every\\n  entry below it in ascending tuple order naming the final winner,\\n  with the off-chain flag recomputed from the final winner. All\\n  landed union assertions were order-free, so only the refusal-census\\n  line pins moved (sessstate.go:924/927 to :929/:932).\\n- GENERATORS: closed small alphabet, hand-written (no new dependency):\\n  exhaustive multisets of size 0..3 with all permutations and all\\n  ordered 2-partitions over three chain shapes, all `Compare`\\n  pairs/triples against an independent builtin-operator oracle, all\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5198,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1300,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
