{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c913","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b074-2d9a-7d23-a683-c8d705b137ba"},"sequence":740,"recorded_at":1780531400001475,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b077bcfc75aebacec2d8e09ce2b8","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260916-n9r71p/TASK-260916-n9r71p_results-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-n9r71p results rev3 — re-derived onto the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry\n2|\n3|Status: implementation complete and fully validated in a post-refresh overlay\n4|tree (27/27 configured commands green, mutants 9/9 + 4/4); candidate left\n5|UNCOMMITTED in the STORY-260916-3uqbwq worktree (15 modified + 3 new files;\n6|`task-board.config.json` shows no diff). The base move itself is NOT done:\n7|`task-board worktree refresh-candidate` refuses because CR rev2 is still\n8|`accepted` (the integration refusals did not demote it), and the two commands\n9|that could establish the precondition (`worktree converge`,\n10|`worktree invalidate-acceptance`) explicitly refuse tracked runs. That step is\n11|operator-only; §1 records the verbatim attempts and the exact operator input\n12|needed. No handoff is made: publishing rev3 at the superseded base would land\n13|at e4e3e88 while a revision is outstanding and re-trigger the same\n14|`validation_suite_changed` refusal.\n15|\n16|## 1. Base-move record (exact commands and OIDs)\n17|\n18|- Trunk: `origin/main = 7efe3854a5a14545f9fa2b7697accb1883249f1f` (verified\n19|  with `git fetch origin` + `git rev-parse origin/main`).\n20|- Story branch `task-board/story/STORY-260916-3uqbwq` tip `9cb5dd4` (replayed\n21|  2yzf5d checkpoint on base `e4e3e88`); lease held by this run\n22|  (`RUN-260917-024356`, confirmed in `worktree status`).\n23|- `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260916-n9r71p` →\n24|  `candidate refresh requires a rework revision; TASK-260916-n9r71p is accepted`\n25|  (retried at three checkpoints; identical refusal every time).\n26|- Why: the rework brief assumed rev2 was demoted to stale by\n27|  `integration_base_moved`. Both integration attempts instead refused with\n28|  `validation_suite_changed` (trunk suite 26→27 commands) with no demotion:\n29|  rev2 is still `accepted` (`worktree obligations`: `accepted / checkpoint`).\n30|- `worktree converge` and `worktree invalidate-acceptance` both refuse tracked\n31|  runs (`transaction_disposition_not_operator` /\n32|  `TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID set ... refused ... on every disposition surface`).\n33|  No producer-side command moves the base; no workaround was attempted (gaming\n34|  the guardrail by unsetting the run id would break the lease the refresh\n35|  itself requires).\n36|\n37|Because the base could not move, every validation below ran in a post-refresh\n38|overlay tree that simulates the exact post-refresh candidate:\n39|\n40|```bash\n41|git clone -s <repo> /tmp/n9r71p-rev3/posttree\n42|git -C /tmp/n9r71p-rev3/posttree checkout 7efe3854a5a14545f9fa2b7697accb1883249f1f\n43|# overlay 1: the 6 checkpoint-only files from HEAD (9cb5dd4)\n44|for f in internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md internal/specdoc/specdoc070_test.go \\\n45|  internal/specpin/pin070_test.go internal/specpin/sections.go \\\n46|  internal/specpin/sections070_test.go internal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json; do\n47|  git show HEAD:$f > posttree/$f\n48|done\n49|# overlay 2: the 18 candidate files (15 modified + 3 new) from the worktree\n50|cp <worktree>/$f posttree/$f  # for each path in git status (scratch excluded)\n51|```\n52|\n53|Post-overlay `git status` shows 24 paths (18 candidate + 6 checkpoint),\n54|matching the whole-Story patch shape. The overlay equals the true\n55|post-refresh tree byte-for-byte provided the refresh (a) replays the\n56|checkpoint with the LOGBOOK resolution in §6 and (b) preserves the candidate\n57|delta bytes — both documented refresh behaviors. §6 proves every other\n58|checkpoint hunk replays cleanly, so the LOGBOOK resolution is the only\n59|operator input the refresh needs beyond the demotion.\n60|\n61|Reran myself in this session (posttree): all 27 configured commands,\n62|26/26 named tests, M0–M8 + R0–R3 mutants, cigate/admission probes, digest\n63|recomputations. Accepted from already-attached evidence: the rev2 ACCEPT\n64|verdict for the 11 files proven byte-identical to the rev2 patch bytes\n65|(§4), and the rev1/rev2 transformation shape (re-applied, not trusted).\n66|\n67|## 2. What changed since rev2\n68|\n69|Rev2 derived `ownership.v0.7.0.json` from the old (e4e3e88) v0.6.0 registry.\n70|Trunk has since landed five v0.6.0-registry stories (315721, 2rqigd, 1oqfec,\n71|1kiyj6 + the PR48 routing change), growing that registry from 101 to 132\n72|acceptance cases and 56 to 65 section bindings. Rev3 re-derives from the\n73|trunk-final registry and merges the trunk test/doc changes under the v0.7.0\n74|delta. Files changed this session (8): `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (rebuilt),\n75|`traceability.go` (digest re-pin only), `traceability_test.go`,\n76|`cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`,\n77|`adoption-v0.7.0.md` (all merged, §3). Untouched and proven byte-identical\n78|to the accepted rev2 bytes (§4): all catalog/cataloggen/cigate/specpin/\n79|specdoc candidate files.\n80|\n81|## 3. Stale-copy audit\n82|\n83|Trunk `e4e3e88..7efe385` touched 229 non-board paths. Intersection with the\n84|candidate: LOGBOOK.md, README.md, `traceability.go`, `traceability_test.go`,\n85|`cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`. (`task-board.config.json` is not a candidate\n86|path and was left untouched; `ownership.v0.5.0/v0.6.0.json` are not candidate\n87|paths and become trunk's bytes automatically at refresh.)\n88|\n89|| 