orktree refresh-candidate TASK-260916-n9r71p` →\n18|  `candidate refresh requires a rework revision; TASK-260916-n9r71p is accepted`\n19|- `task-board worktree converge STORY-260916-3uqbwq --reason <text>` →\n20|  `transaction_disposition_not_operator: TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID is set, so this is a spawned run\n21|  rather than an operator; worktree converge rewrites the Story branch a tracked run stands\n22|  on and is refused from one as a guardrail; it authorizes nothing on its own`\n23|- `worktree obligations`: `TASK-260916-n9r71p rev 2 accepted / checkpoint`; `worktree status`:\n24|  Story tip `9cb5dd4`, tree dirty (18 paths), lease held by this run; `transaction show`: none.\n25|- Root cause (unchanged since the prior run): the rework brief assumed rev2 reached `stale`\n26|  via `integration_base_moved`. Both bound integration attempts (RUN-260917-6b4417,\n27|  RUN-260917-69703d; outcomes `TASK-260916-n9r71p_integration-outcome-rev2.md` and\n28|  `TASK-260916-n9r71p_integration-attempt-rev2_outcome.md`) instead refused with\n29|  `validation_suite_changed` (trunk suite 26→27 commands: +rpcwire fuzz, PR48 routing),\n30|  which opens no transaction and demotes nothing.\n31|\n32|Failed assumption: \"refresh-candidate will work because the integration attempt ran\".\n33|It ran twice and refused at admission both times, so the rework-revision precondition\n34|for refresh was never established.\n35|\n36|Alternatives considered and rejected:\n37|- Handoff rev3 now → CR construction runs the control-root (new-trunk) suite on the\n38|  old-base candidate tree; trunk-landed files (sessprofile, rpcwire) are absent, so\n39|  construction fails. Rejected: publishes a known-broken revision.\n40|- Unset TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID to dodge the converge guardrail → breaks the Story lease the\n41|  refresh itself requires, and games an explicit safety guardrail. Rejected.\n42|- Hand-rebase the Story branch → forbidden (no commits on the Story branch; handoff\n43|  requires tip == recorded checkpoint `9cb5dd4`). Rejected.\n44|- Chosen: operator (untracked shell) runs converge; then a leased producer run finishes\n45|  refresh → validate → handoff (§4).\n46|\n47|## 2. Inherited rev3 bytes (verified, not trusted)\n48|\n49|Worktree `git status` is exactly the 18 §7 paths of `TASK-260916-n9r71p_results-rev3.md`\n50|(15 modified + 3 new; `task-board.config.json` clean; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`/strays):\n51|\n52|- `sha256(internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json)` =\n53|  `2548870d896b0e119c307cdcba02ab23b36af7f473328a15f6a092090d8a5070` (matches §7).\n54|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in `traceability.go` =\n55|  `c4cd46bf71f164ad53dfe00ddd2e64e0b439e1c2684138fbcfe208f7e53473f6` (matches §4).\n56|- P3 fix present: `Disclosure owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.` in the 11.10.5 gap;\n57|  19 remaining `Pending implementation owner` hits are the STORY-owner gaps (expected).\n58|\n59|## 3. Overlay re-validation (reran myself this session)\n60|\n61|Rebuilt `/tmp/n9r71p-verify/posttree` with the exact §1 recipe of results-rev3.md:\n62|clone, checkout `7efe3854`, overlay the 6 checkpoint-only files from `HEAD`, overlay the\n63|18 candidate files from the worktree. Post-overlay status: 24 paths; ownership sha256\n64|identical to §2. Results:\n65|\n66|| Check | Result |\n67|| --- | --- |\n68|| `gofmt -l` over candidate Go files | clean (no output), exit 0 |\n69|| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n70|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | exit 0, `acceptance_cases=135 bindings=68 clauses_discharged=49/569` (exact rev3 figures) |\n71|| `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | exit 0, empty output |\n72|| Affected packages (`traceability/...`, `catalog/...`, `cataloggen/...`, `cigate/...`, `specpin/...`, `specdoc/...`) `-count=1` | 8/8 `ok` (tracecheck suite 106s) |\n73|| All remaining 29 packages `-count=1` | 29/29 `ok`, `go test` exit 0, no FAIL/panic |\n74|| Pre-refresh worktree tracecheck (base-move evidence) | fails closed, verbatim: `acceptance case \"sessprofile-derive\" production owner: read \"internal/sessprofile/profile.go\": ... no such file or directory` |\n75|\n76|Total: 37/37 packages green in the overlay, matching the rev3 record.\n77|\n78|Accepted from already-attached evidence (NOT rerun by this run): mutants M0–M8 + R0–R3,\n79|14 fuzz gates, `-race`/`-cover` suites, cross-compiles, `task-board validate`, historical\n80|file byte-identity proofs, owner-story board queries, replay-resolution byte proofs.\n81|Rationale: this run's scope is blocker verification + independent green confirmation of\n82|the candidate bytes; the accepted items are byte-stable artifacts of the unchanged tree.\n83|\n84|## 4. Exact operator input needed (resumes the leaf, no product decision pending)\n85|\n86|From a shell WITHOUT `TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID`:\n87|\n88|1. `git fetch origin` (confirm still `7efe3854…`; if trunk moved again, the overlay\n89|   prediction must be rebuilt — the recipe in §3 is exact).\n90|2. `task-board worktree converge STORY-260916-3uqbwq --reason '<operator reason>'`\n91|3. From a live leased producer run: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate\n92|   TASK-260916-n9r71p`, then retry with `--replay-resolutions` built from\n93|   `replay-resolutions.json` inside `TASK-260916-n9r71p_producer-evidence-rev3.tar.gz`\n94|   (LOGBOOK is the only conflict; `version`/`candidate_tree_oid` from the retained\n95|   replay template; `checkpoint_oid`/`path`/`sha256`/`content` final).\n96|4. Re-run the 27-command suite on the refreshed tree (this outcome predicts green),\n97|   then `task-board handoff TASK-260916-n9r71p --role developer`.\n98|\n99|State left by this run: worktree untouched (18 uncommitted paths, tip `9cb5dd4`, no\n100|commits); `/tmp/n9r71p-verify` removed; no board mutations except this outcome and the\n101|`blocked` routing stop.","final_result":true}}}
