coverage — 3fjjtn parsing/refusals (14.1, 13.1, contract), 2q85nu record embedding (5.1), 1kp1lx stdin/replay (7.5), 1ea7od plugin capability (7.3/7.4), 3aukw3 drift (13.10), 3ustb3 naming (13.1 split), vucwn0 vectors (fixture, appendix-d split). The source-derived AdoptedSections test requires 6/6 plus 2 split attributions and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections.\\n> - HISTORY: registry re-derived from the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry, carrying the five landed stories' 31 acceptance cases and 9 section bindings (2.2, 2.4, 5.3/5.4/5.5, 6.6, 7.7, 8, 10.6, 11.10.1–4, 13.12/13.13, 16.1) with re-measured clause lines; v0.6.0/v0.5.0 locks, registries, readers and historical tests byte-untouched versus trunk; the v0.7.0 inventory is identifier-equal to v0.6.0 (170 ids, same digest), so legacy verification derives both historical registries from the adopted lock. P3 closed: pin.go/specdoc.go consumer comments now true in the present tense; section:11.10.5 carried as a Disclosure owner (source evidence only, no implementation claim).\\n> - FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n> - STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n433a442,450\\n> ### TASK-260916-2yzf5d: adopted signed v0.7.0 normative source alongside v0.5.0/v0.6.0, no consumer re-pointed\\n> - PROVENANCE (verified this session, upstream read-only): `git tag -v v0.7.0` Good (tag object `d4abe46f…795b3`, ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM`, tagger Ivan Oparin), peeled commit `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC.md blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes SHA256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` measured from the tagged blob (zero CR bytes, raw == LF-normalized).\\n> - SCOPE: `internal/specpin/{pin,sections}.go` + `v0.7.0.lock.json` (64 contracts, 6 fixtures), `internal/specdoc/{specdoc.go,SPEC.v0.7.0.md}` + `pin070_test.go`, `sections070_test.go`, `specdoc070_test.go`, README provenance paragraphs, this entry. `v0.5.0`/`v0.6.0` locks, documents, readers and all existing tests byte-untouched in behavior.\\n> - DELTA (measured, SPEC §1.5 cross-checked row-for-row in order, lock registry verified against the spec table by script): +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (between Session record and Session event); Session record +3.1.0, Provider protocol +2.1.0/+3.1.0, Provider manifest/probe +1.1.0, Structured error +1.5.0, CLI result unchanged at 5.0.0; +0 numbered sections (only an unnumbered `#### Caller launch-plan code` and appendix subsection A.12, both excluded by the inventory rule — the 170-identifier inventory digest is measured equal to v0.6.0's and pinned independently); +1 fixture (`ax-launch-plan-request-v1` `ec4310b8…`), host-channel/selector fixture digests move for a `specification_version` 0.7.0 bump only, 3 old fixture files byte-identical upstream. v0.4.3 compatibility grows to 9 absent + 9 overrides exactly as the v0.7.0 historical account states.\\n> - HISTORY: v0.7.0 projections of v0.6.0 (63 rows), v0.5.0 (60 rows) and v0.4.3 (55 rows) are `reflect.DeepEqual` to the real locks/projections — adoption cannot rewrite history. `ContractsForRelease(v0.7.0)` on a v0.5.0 or v0.6.0 manifest is refused: a stale pin cannot authorize the new release. Launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift runtime support is not claimed; `catalog/`, `traceability/`, `cigate/`, `localstore/` untouched, `tracecheck` still 17/463, `cataloggen -check` green without regeneration.\\n> - MUTANTS (5 narrowing, each admits exactly one member end-to-end, each kills exactly its named subtest, full suites otherwise green, all restored snapshot-clean): M1 identity+stale-commit, M2 token-preserving delta-row Versions drop (full behavioral suite under plant), M3 ParseV070+stale-v0.6.0-doc, M4 projection serves v0.7.0 from stale manifest, M5 digest+trailing-newline; M0 harmless operand-swap SURVIVED. VerifyV070 is layered (validate then digest), so M1/M2/M5 span both layers with precomputed digests. Harness + raw logs in the task evidence tarball.\\n> - DEPENDENCY: catalogue/traceability regeneration is sibling TASK-260916-n9r71p, after this leaf checkpoints. `Current`/`Verify`/`Load` intentionally still serve v0.5.0; v0.6.0 consumers move with the sibling, not here.\\n> - STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n> \\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10987,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2747,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"failure"}}}
