6.0.md`, `pin060_test.go`, `sections060_test.go`,\n53|  `specdoc060_test.go`, `pin_test.go`, `specdoc_test.go` — empty diff vs base.\n54|  Unchanged v060/v050 suites (16 top-level tests) green against the new code;\n55|  v0.7.0→v0.6.0/v0.5.0/v0.4.3 projections `reflect.DeepEqual` to real locks.\n56|- No production consumer outside specpin/specdoc touches a V070 entry yet\n57|  (grep over `internal/`); catalog/traceability/localstore untouched — correct\n58|  per scope precedent (sibling TASK-260916-n9r71p owns re-pointing).\n59|\n60|## 4. Refusal census — 12/12 AC rows driven; my 6 adversarial plants refused\n61|\n62|Committed tests drive every arm through production entries\n63|(`specpin.VerifyV070`, `specdoc.ParseV070`, `Manifest.ContractsForRelease`):\n64|wrong tag / stale tag-object / stale commit (tokens preserved) / wrong digest /\n65|forged inventory / trimmed delta / dropped row / forged namespace / substituted\n66|+ stale-host-channel fixture digests / capability claim / partial-malformed-byte\n67|reads / cross-version bytes / stale-pin authorization / unknown releases —\n68|all `ErrPinMismatch` / `ErrUnsupportedRelease` as appropriate.\n69|My plants (sandbox, production entries): trailing-space tag → refused\n70|(identity drift); 7-char-prefix zero-padded commit → refused; uppercase-hex\n71|document digest → refused; reordered contract rows → refused (digest layer —\n72|semantic layer passes by design, proving the layering); CRLF document →\n73|refused; trailing-newline document → refused. 6/6 refused.\n74|\n75|## 5. Mutations — producer harness rerun 3×; 4 own narrowing mutants killed\n76|\n77|- Producer `mutate.sh` in the sandbox copy: M1–M5 KILLED each by exactly its\n78|  named subtest (full suites otherwise green), M0 SURVIVED — 3/3 runs,\n79|  `pass=6 fail=0`, tree restored snapshot-clean every run.\n80|- Own mutants (arms the producer did not touch), each with a reviewer-owned\n81|  killer probe that PASSES on the clean tree: R1 tag case-insensitive