nager-spec`:\n23|  `git status` clean, HEAD `32b3f2ba` (unmodified).\n24|\n25|## 2. Section inventory — reproduced with an independent extractor\n26|\n27|- Heading-text diff v0.6.0→v0.7.0: title bump + exactly 2 additions —\n28|  `### A.12 Curator launch-plan revision traceability` and\n29|  `#### Caller launch-plan code`. No numbered section added/removed/renamed.\n30|- My extractor (numbered headings + 4 appendix slugs, appendix subsections\n31|  excluded) yields 170 ids, digest `2ef110e0…` for BOTH documents — identical\n32|  files — and is ELEMENT-WISE equal to production `SectionInventoryV070()`\n33|  (dumped in the sandbox copy, `diff` empty).\n34|- No citable-but-missing section: new content resolves inside 15.3 / A.12\n35|  (committed `TestSectionIDResolvesV070Clauses` pins lines 15302/15309→15.3,\n36|  16518/16530→A.12). Identity never rests on inventory alone: stale v0.6.0\n37|  bytes are refused by the `ParseV070` digest gate.\n38|\n39|## 3. Lock registry — reproduced with an independent extractor\n40|\n41|- My §1.5-table extractor vs `v0.7.0.lock.json`: 64 rows, ORDER-identical,\n42|  name/urn/version SET-identical. One presentation-order note (not a defect):\n43|  spec prose lists Provider-protocol versions `2.0.0, 3.0.0, 2.1.0, 3.1.0`\n44|  while the lock normalizes to strictly increasing\n45|  `2.0.0, 2.1.0, 3.0.0, 3.1.0` — the gate itself (`validateVersions`) requires\n46|  strictly increasing order, and the delta test pins the sorted list.\n47|- Launch Plan request row sits between Session record and Session event\n48|  (spec-table order, committed position test). v0.4.3 historical account in\n49|  the spec text matches `expectedAbsentContractsV070` (9) /\n50|  `expectedVersionOverridesV070` (9) exactly.\n51|- History intact: `v0.5.0.lock.json`, `v0.6.0.lock.json`, `SPEC.md`,\n52|  `SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, `pin060_test.go`, `sections060_test.go`,\n53|  `specdoc060_test.go`, `pin_test.go`, `specdoc_test.go` — empty diff vs base.\n54|  Unchanged v060/v050 suites (16 top-level tests) green against the new code;\n55|  v0.7.0→v0.6.0/v0.5.0/v0.4.3 projections `reflect.DeepEqual` to real locks.\n56|- No production consumer outside specpin/specdoc touches a V070 entry yet\n57|  (grep over `internal/`); catalog/traceability/localstore untouched — correct\n58|  per scope precedent (sibling TASK-260916-n9r71p owns re-pointing).\n59|\n60|## 4. Refusal census — 12/12 AC rows driven; my 6 adversarial plants refused\n61|\n62|Committed tests drive every arm through production entries\n63|(`specpin.VerifyV070`, `specdoc.ParseV070`, `Manifest.ContractsForRelease`):\n64|wrong tag / stale tag-object / stale commit (tokens preserved) / wrong digest /\n65|forged inventory / trimmed delta / dropped row / forged namespace / substituted\n66|+ stale-host-channel fixture digests / capability claim / partial-malformed-byte\n67|reads / cross-version bytes / stale-pin authorization / unknown releases —\n68|all `ErrPinMismatch` / `ErrUnsupportedRelease` as appropriate.\n69|My plants (sandbox, production entries): trailing-space tag → refused\n70|(identity drift); 7-char-prefix zero-padded commit → refused; uppercase-hex\n71|document digest → refused; reordered contract rows → refused (digest layer —\n72|semantic layer passes by design, proving the layering); CRLF document →\n73|refused; trailing-newline document → refused. 6/6 refused.\n74|\n75|## 5. Mutations — producer harness rerun 3×; 4 own narrowing mutants killed\n76|\n77|- Producer `mutate.sh` in the sandbox copy: M1–M5 KILLED each by exactly its\n78|  named subtest (full suites otherwise green), M0 SURVIVED — 3/3 runs,\n79|  `pass=6 fail=0`, tree restored snapshot-clean every run.\n80|- Own mutants (arms the producer did not touch), each with a reviewer-owned\n81|  killer probe that PASSES on the clean tree: R1 tag case-insensitive\n82|  (admits `V0.7.0`) — KILLED; R2 row-count `< 63` (admits 63-row\n83|  dropped-Lease lock; the committed dropped-row test still passes, proving\n84|  narrowing) — KILLED; R3 delta versions major.minor-only (admits\n85|  `3.1.99`) — KILLED; R4 digest 5-hex-char prefix (admits a ground,\n86|  semantically-neutral, prefix-sharing member, digest `5696ce73…`) — KILLED.\n87|  Each by exactly its named probe (1 FAIL line, full `specpin` suite green\n88|  otherwise). R0 operand-swap control SURVIVED. 5/5 as designed.\n89|\n90|## 6. Gates on the exact tree (observed exits)\n91|\n92|`gofmt -l internal` empty 0; `go vet ./...` 0; `go build ./...` 0;\n93|`go test ./... -count=1` 0 (all packages ok, 0 FAIL);\n94|`go test -cover` 0 (specpin 87.8%, specdoc 100.0%);\n95|`go test -race ./internal/specpin/ ./internal/specdoc/` 0;\n96|`tracecheck` 0 (17/463 unchanged); `cataloggen … -check` (configured command,\n97|verbatim) 0, `catalog_gen.go` untouched.\n98|\n99|## 7. Docs / scope notes\n100|\n101|- README/LOGBOOK make no launch-plan/stdin/`caller_launch_plan`/\n102|  `environment_drift` runtime claim — the README carries an explicit\n103|  non-claim paragraph; `unsupported_capability_claim` is refused by the gate.\n104|- P3 (non-blocking, recorded, no change requested): `pin.go`'s v0.7.0 comment\n105|  says catalogue/traceability/CI \"consume v0.7.0 through CurrentV070\" — true\n106|  only after sibling n9r71p re-points (README states it precisely; same\n107|  forward-looking shape as the accepted v0.6.0 adoption).\n108|- What n9r71p must re-point: catalog directive + `catalog.v0.7.0.json` +\n109|  `catalog_gen.go` (via `cataloggen -contracts v0.7.0.lock.json`, then\n110|  `-check`); traceability `LoadV060`→`LoadV070` + census denominator;\n111|  cigate contract roots; localstore stays on `CurrentV050` (intentional).\n112|\n113|## Verdict: ACCEPT revision 1\n114|\n115|AC coverage 12 of 12 rows driven through production entry points, no stated\n116|bounds. No P1/P2 findings; two P3 observations recorded above. Evidence:\n117|`TASK-260916-2yzf5d_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (provenance transcript, gate\n118|log, extractor scripts/output