{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d21b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b074-2d9a-7d23-a683-c8d705b137ba"},"sequence":1896,"recorded_at":1780531400003787,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b07f-aa25-79c3-abb3-f5871883d8c4"},"task_id":"01a0b07f-aa25-79c3-abb3-f5871883d8c4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b07f-aa25-79c3-abb3-f5871883d8c4","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-64-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nold=json.load(open('/tmp/verify-10k118/ownership.v0.6.0.trunk.json'))\\nnew=json.load(open('/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260917-110onn/worktree/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json'))\\ndef gap(d,key):\\n    for g in d['ownership']:\\n        if g['kind']=='section_binding' and g['keys']==[key]: return g.get('gap','')\\nfor k in ['section:appendix-d','section:5.1','section:7.3','section:7.4','section:7.5']:\\n    print('=== '+k+' OLD:'); print(gap(old,k)); print('--- NEW:'); print(gap(new,k)); print()\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Show five gap updates old vs new\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"=== section:appendix-d OLD:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference Appendix D; no clause of Appendix D is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 16 obligations it carries.\\n--- NEW:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference Appendix D; no clause of Appendix D is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 18 obligations it carries. The Launch Plan request fixture row is pending STORY-260916-vucwn0 vectors.\\n\\n=== section:5.1 OLD:\\nvalidateSessionRecordWithDerivation validates the Section 5.1 Session Record shape; the derivation and lifecycle behaviour Section 5.1 requires is not implemented and no clause of Section 5.1 is enumerated.\\n--- NEW:\\nvalidateSessionRecordWithDerivation validates the Section 5.1 Session Record shape; the derivation and lifecycle behaviour Section 5.1 requires is not implemented, and the Launch Stdin member, the Curator extension keys and the fragment-digest rule Section 5.1 adds are not implemented, so no clause of Section 5.1 is enumerated. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-2q85nu.\\n\\n=== section:7.3 OLD:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.3; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 7.3, because the closed Provider Manifest states its obligations as a required-member table, a 16-entry operation registry and exactly 7 capability names rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure this section - and the closed manifest is implemented in internal/provhost DecodeManifest, exercised by the provhost conformance suite.\\n--- NEW:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.3; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 7.3, because the closed Provider Manifest states its obligations as a required-member table, a 16-entry operation registry and a nine-name capability registry (seven names under 1.0.0) rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure this section - and the 1.1.0 caller_launch_plan and stdin_resume_replay names are unimplemented. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1ea7od; the seven-name 1.0.0 manifest stays implemented in internal/provhost DecodeManifest, exercised by the provhost conformance suite.\\n\\n=== section:7.4 OLD:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.4; no clause of 7.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 1 obligations it carries.\\n--- NEW:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.4; the 1.1.0 probe response with nine capability keys is unimplemented, and no clause of 7.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 1 obligation it carries. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1ea7od.\\n\\n=== section:7.5 OLD:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.5; the host-side Section 7.5 operation conformance (SpawnPlan launch and resume bodies, identify-session results, materialize-status recovery, and the single operation plus operation_id mutation key) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, and no clause of Section 7.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 53 obligations it carries.\\n--- NEW:\\nForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.5; the host-side Section 7.5 operation conformance (SpawnPlan launch and resume bodies, identify-session results, materialize-status recovery, and the single operation plus operation_id mutation key) is implemented in internal/provhost under the Section 7.6 and Section 7.7 bindings, the SpawnPlan.stdin member, the resume.launch_plan member and the stdin replay rule are unimplemented, and no clause of Section 7.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 56 obligations it carries. Pending implementation owner: STORY-260916-1kp1lx.\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4142,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1036,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
