{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e619","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b074-2d9a-7d23-a683-c8d705b137ba"},"sequence":4455,"recorded_at":1780531400008905,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a105643e-74d8-47fc-98b0-dd8b6640f48f"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Handed off to review. `TASK-260917-10k118` is `to-review`, checklist 14/14, with three outcome resources attached.\n\n## What was done\n\nReconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk `7efe385` in the managed Story worktree, left uncommitted (16 modified + 10 new paths, branch tip unchanged, `task-board.config.json` equals HEAD).\n\nKey reconstruction decision: the exported 238-file pin patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so the true 10-file pin delta (`e4e3e88..9cb5dd4`) was applied instead, plus the 15-file registry patch and 3 untracked files. All 19 machine-applied files are `cmp`-identical to the accepted rev3 bytes; the 5 trunk-merged files were diff-reviewed (no trunk test lost).\n\n## Verification (all re-run this session)\n\n- Provenance from a fresh clone: tag Good, SPEC sha256 `c6b2fe64…`, byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n- Lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table; exactly +1 ID, 0 removals\n- Registry: 65/65 bindings and 132/132 cases carried, 49/49 clauses re-measured via production helpers (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392), digest `c4cd46bf…` recomputed two independent ways, registry reproduction byte-identical\n- New `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport`, both green\n- Mutants: pin 6/6, registry 9/9, new-test 10/10 (incl. token-preserving R3 with full behavioral suites); controls survived\n- Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree (37/37 packages, race clean, 14/14 fuzz)\n- AC coverage 30 of 30 rows driven with named call sites in the conformance matrix\n\n## Findings (in LOGBOOK and results)\n\n- F1: reviewed v0.7.0 source group keeps production `VerifyV060` though its cases moved to v0.7.0 — pinned literally, fix recommended as follow-up\n- Reviewed prose says \"48 carried clause lines\"; measured 49 (artifact correct)\n- No runtime capability claimed anywhere","reason":null}}
